---
description: Architecture design session guardrails. Enable only while the target-design review is running; delete afterwards.
alwaysApply: true
---

An architecture design review is in progress. These override normal behavior.

- Writes permitted ONLY under `docs/architecture/target/out/` and `tools/arch/`.
  Any diff to `src/`, `tests/`, `alphas/`, `configs/` is a protocol violation.
- Do not fix anything you find. Record it as a finding. Fixing is a later session.
- Every material claim cites `path:symbol` or `path:line` and is labeled
  VERIFIED (read the code) / INFERRED (derived) / ASSUMED (not checkable).
- Prefer running a script under `tools/arch/` and citing its evidence file over
  reading files and reporting numbers. A number you did not measure is not VERIFIED.
- Code is truth; documentation is a claim. Report disagreements; do not resolve
  them silently or prefer the doc.
- Stop at the phase hard stop. Do not begin the next phase.
- On ambiguity: ask exactly one specific question and stop. Do not guess.
- No status called "working". Use specified / implemented / conformance-tested /
  open defect.
